sane-backends 1.4.0's xerox_mfp backend offers the scan sources "Flatbed",
"ADF" and "Auto" on every device, although dev_inquiry() already reads from
the INQUIRY reply whether the device has a document feeder (dev->has_adf).
Frontends such as AirSane then advertise an ADF on flatbed-only models.

With this change the source option offers only "Flatbed" when has_adf is
false; has_adf is set before init_options() runs. dev_inquiry() also logs
has_adf at debug level 3. Not sent upstream yet (an upstream merge request
would also bump BACKEND_BUILD). Drop this patch once Ubuntu's sane-backends
has the change.

